    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFix two speculative-decoding drafter failures in ROCm AITER FlashAttention (ROCM_AITER_FA): handle zero-chunk extend steps in AiterFlashAttentionImpl.extend_forward without calling merge_attn_states on None, and size AiterFlashAttentionMetadataBuilder workspaces from kv_cache_spec rather than the target model's model_config.\n\nFixes #64680\n\n## Claims\n\n- Fixes AttributeError in merge_attn_states when AiterFlashAttentionImpl.extend_forward runs on an extend step with num_chunks == 0 (for example during drafter warmup when there is no cached prefix context).\n- Fixes out-of-bounds KV gather writes in cp_mha_gather_cache when a speculative-decoding drafter KV-cache group has a different per-rank num_kv_heads or head_size than the target model.\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\npytest tests/models/test_muse_spark_rocm_loading.py -v\n```\n\n## Details\n\n1. In AiterFlashAttentionImpl.extend_forward, chunked_output and chunked_lse remain None when num_chunks == 0 (an extend batch with no cached context blocks). Copy out directly into output when chunked_output is None instead of invoking merge_attn_states with prefix_output=None.\n2. In AiterFlashAttentionMetadataBuilder.__init__, read num_heads_kv and headdim from the group's kv_cache_spec rather than vllm_config.model_config so extend_workspace, swa_workspace, and ASM KV scale tables match the drafter group's KV geometry.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's /pr-checklist skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
